     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"The target is an OR of h3_0:access, h3_1:reach and h3_2:reach, so all three must be made unreachable. Blocking h1_1:access cuts off h3_2:reach, since h1_1:access is its only parent. It also cuts off h3_1:reach, an AND step that needs h1_1:access. h3_0:access does not depend on h1_1:access: it is reachable through h1_0:reach and h2_1:reach, which both get input directly from edge1:reach. So h3_0:access must be blocked itself. No single block works, because h3_2:reach depends only on h1_1:access while h3_0:access is independent of it. The minimum is therefore 2: {h1_1:access, h3_0:access}.\"}"
    }
